
// First encounter with Ekilis in room #1
@1=~You thought you could attack me by surprise! (looks around, finally surprised)~
@2=~Tell me where that bitch Systera is, I don't care about her lackeys!~
@3=~We're nobody's lackeys! What were you doing here in stasis?~ 
@4=~You're pretty sure of yourself. Why don't you show us how you're going to die instead!~
@5=~Just simple adventurers then...~
@6=~My name is Karl and I'm here for the same reasons as you, my brave ones. I'm looking for the treasure of Bhaal, the dead god!~ 
@7=~It doesn't matter... Killing has never been a problem for me. (predatory smile)~ 
@8=~You will join me and each of you will have your share of the loot.~ @9=~That's fine with me, but there are more of us, so you're coming with us.~ 
@10=~That's fine with me. Let's go!~ 
@11=~We don't need you. You can leave.~
@12=~I don't want to. And I don't want you to stay alive either.~
@13=~As a child of Bhaal, you'll understand that I don't much like people coming to plunder my temple...~ 
@14=~Don't be ridiculous, my friend. I don't want to play the "mine's bigger than yours" game. You'd be the loser. Let's go! We don't have time to waste.~ 
@15=~I wouldn't bet on your survival without me. In fact, you're already dead. Farewell!~ 
@16=~It's alright... Killing has never been a problem for me. (predatory grin)~ 
@17=~So the rumor was true... Bhaal has kids! (laughs)~ 
@18=~For your information, my real name is Ekilis, the Grand Inquisitor. Cyric will generously reward me for your head!~
@19=~What do you want?~ 
@20=~Who is this Systera?~ 
@21=~Did you come to the temple alone?~ 
@22=~The same thing happened to us... We're trapped just like you.~ 
@23=~Just so you know, the door has closed again. But we've met a ghost who's ready to help us. We must first take its remains to a gate.~
@24=~What can you tell us about the temple?~
@25=~Why were you in stasis?~
@26=~Systera serves Bhaal. She is the guardian of the temple despite the disappearance of her master. She prowls the area.~ 
@27=~My companions died while we were exploring the place. Their lack of caution was fatal.~
@28=~Ah... Well, in that case, we'll find a way out of here once we've found the treasure! I'm fed up with this temple...~
@29=~(contained surprise) That's excellent news. All we have to do now is find the treasure then.~ 
@30=~Beware of the gates and walls; there are often traps, and sometimes creatures appear out of nowhere. I advise you to keep your eyes peeled.~ 
@31=~The temple door closed behind us, and I couldn't find another way out. But now that you're here, it means the door is open again!~ 
@32=~The Treasure of Bhaal I discovered Karl in stasis in the temple of Bhaal.As I approached, he emerged from stasis, ready for battle. He thought we were lackeys of 'Systera'! Karl claims a treasure is hidden in the temple. We formed an alliance to find it together.~
@33=~The Treasure of Bhaal I discovered Karl in stasis in the Temple of Bhaal. As I approached, he emerged from his stasis, ready for battle. He thought we were lackeys of 'Systera'! Karl claims a treasure is hidden in the temple. I refused his offer of an alliance to share the treasure. I will find it without him!~ 
@34=~The Treasure of Bhaal I discovered Karl in stasis in the Temple of Bhaal. As I approached, he emerged from his stasis, ready for battle. He thought we were lackeys of 'Systera'! Karl claims a treasure is hidden in the temple. I refused his offer of an alliance and decided to get rid of him. I will find the treasure without him.~ 
@35=~The Treasure of Bhaal I discovered Karl in stasis in the Temple of Bhaal. As I approached, he emerged from stasis, ready for battle. He thought we were lackeys of 'Systera'! Karl claims that a treasure is hidden in the temple. I decided to get rid of him. One does not plunder the temple of my late father with impunity! That made him laugh. Karl is actually Ekilis, the Grand Inquisitor of Cyric. He is already looking forward to taking my head.~
@36=~How do you know there is a treasure?~ 
@37=~If my experience is anything to go by, when a place is kept secret, it is because it holds riches. All that remains is to find the place.~ 
@38=~Follow us!~
@39=~The Treasure of Bhaal Massena accused my new companion Karl of being a servant of Cyric. Karl categorically denies it. Who to believe?~ //Massena demands Ekilis's death @60=~Gold is my only master, and no one will stop me from finding Bhaal's treasure. Not even a ghost!~ @61=~Let's continue! I have a feeling we're on the right track to making a fortune.~ @62=~A loyal follower of Cyric, that makes sense... Too bad for you!~ @63=~We have his remains with me if that can be useful in getting rid of him.~ @64=~Onward, I don't have time to waste on this nonsense!~ @65=~Excellent, soon we won't have this parasite on our backs anymore.~ @66=~I have a feeling we're going to regret this soon...~ // Ekilis meets Systera @67=~I'm going to dismember you piece by piece. SYSTERA!~ @68=~You should have accepted this slow death!~ // Meeting at the well with Massena @90=~Why continue to serve a god who no longer exists? Recognize Cyric, the god of gods, and enter his service. He will grant you powers far beyond what you can imagine...~ //@90=~Ekilis, Cyric's grand inquisitor, has come to finish off your pathetic master hiding in this hole...~ @91=~What a waste, don't you think? This time we'll eliminate him!~ //@91=~Cyric will recognize my inestimable worth and I will be rewarded!~ // Arriving at the well, Massena was burned by Ekilis. @92=~So this is where Bhaal is hiding, crouching in a hole... It's pathetic (predatory smile)~ @93=~Bhaal is dead, he cannot be here.~ @94=~His followers have spoken, he is dying in this place and I am the only one who knows it!~ @95=~(he turns towards the well) I, Ekilis, the Grand Inquisitor of Cyric, have come to finish you off and your vile offspring will disappear at the same time! (He brandishes a purple skull like a trophy, his eyes wild)~ @96=~Cyric will recognize my inestimable worth, and I will be rewarded with terrifying powers!~ @97=~But what about the treasure and the loot?~ @98=~Don't bother me with your trivial question. Witness my victory! One last incantation, and the hour of my coronation will have struck!~ @99=~It's a fine story, but I have a better ending for you. Bhaal is my father, and I will offer him your corpse!~ @100=~So your presence was no accident. Very well, I'll start with you, Bhaal's pup. Then I'll finish off your whole family!~ /* // Massena is dead and the well is discovered @92=~Excellent, the well is finally discovered and that insignificant priest is dead.~ @93=~You served me well, but Ekilis, Cyric's Grand Inquisitor, no longer needs you... DISAPPEAR! (crazy look)~ @94=~Ekilis, Cyric's Grand Inquisitor, now only has to eliminate Bhaal's puppy!~ */ // DisplayStringHead @500=~We'll avoid the middle chest if possible...~doesn't need you anymore... DISAPPEAR! (crazy stare)~ @94=~Ekilis, Cyric's Grand Inquisitor, only has to eliminate Bhaal's puppy!~ */ // DisplayStringHead @500=~We'll avoid the middle chest if possible...~doesn't need you anymore... DISAPPEAR! (crazy stare)~ @94=~Ekilis, Cyric's Grand Inquisitor, only has to eliminate Bhaal's puppy!~ */ // DisplayStringHead 
@500=~We'll avoid the middle chest if possible...~
